   "design": "Staff request supplies through a form that feeds one list per building in the university purchasing system ({PROCUREMENT}), so requests are not collected from e-mails. The contract catalogue shows contract prices for about 70% of order lines, so the advisor compares prices only for the rest, and the order is built from the catalogue items. Once checked, the order goes to the supplier from the system. Deciding what to order and checking deliveries stay with the advisor.",
   "previous_blocker": "Requests came by e-mail and prices were compared site by site.",
   "enabler_now": "Purchasing systems hold contract catalogues and send orders.",
   "still_hard": "Special items outside the catalogue still need quotes.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which supplies run out in exam weeks.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Nothing changes.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "residence staff",
     "task": "Request supplies",
     "learn": "Whether requests are met sooner."
    }
   ],
   "build_days": {
